{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/831929-many-shades-of-surrender","id":831929,"title":"Many shades of surrender","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-17T11:47:33-08:00","id":831929,"title":"Many shades of surrender","content":"I have a player that really enjoys the idea of the red surrender and we've been trying to bring it into Blood and Smoke.<br /> <br /> We discussed that we believe the idea of the beast has changed from the Clan book to now. Before there was only one type of beast and now with Blood and Smoke there is at least three.<br /> <br /> I'd like to come up with three different surrenders, one for each beast, presented on page 90 of Blood and smoke.<br /> <br /> The Black Surrender ( Monstrous beast)<br /> <br /> The Green Surrender (Seductive Beast)<br /> <br /> The Red Surrender (Competitive Beast)<br /> <br /> We went with Red being the Competitive Beast seeing as its the Alpha mind set is more beastial/animalistic rather then Monstrous Beast which seemed to be less animal and more just monster, fear for sake of fear, but I'm open for suggestions.<br /> <br /> A rough working idea we have is inspired by <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender\"> B&amp;S Red Surrender - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Has it been discussed and will it make a return? Always thought it was an interesting thing and was toying with a coil based around the premise of the characters higher mind and the beast working together to improve their survival. Just curious. Thanks. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> [Will post various conditions next post]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T13:56:07-08:00","id":832045,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Black Surrender<br /> <br /> The Instinct (</span>Monstrous<span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span><br /> You've leaned to feel your beast rather then cage it away. Subtract one die from any rolls to resist frenzy. She gains the 9-again quality on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Stealth rolls. She loses the 10-again quality on Empathy, Expression, Socialize, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls.<br /> <br /> No longer able to lash out with Competitive or Seductive beast.<br /> <br /> Your character will leave The Instinct Surrender and enter The Voice Surrender after one week. This does not give a Beat.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Successfully resist frenzy; if so, leave The Surrender.<br /> <br /> <b>Other Possible Resolution</b>: Gain a dot in Blood Potency, commit Aramanth; if so, enter The Whisper<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Whisper (</span>Monstrous<span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span><br /> You've gotten closer to your beast, you can hear it whisper just at the edge of thought. Subtract two dice from any roll to resist frenzy. Subtract one die from any roll to resist Detachment. Raise her effective Blood Potency by one dot. She gains the 9-again quality on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Stealth rolls. She cannot achieve exceptional successes on Empathy, Expression, Socialize, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls, and loses 10-again.<br /> <br /> No longer able to lash out with Competitive or Seductive beast. Lashing out with Monstrous Beast gains 9 again<br /> <br /> Your character will leave The Whisper and enter The Voice Surrender after one week. This does not give a Beat.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Successfully resist frenzy; if so, leave The Surrender.<br /> <br /> <b>Other Possible Resolution</b>: Gain a dot in Blood Potency, commit Aramanth; if so, Enter The Voice<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Voice (</span>Monstrous<span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span><br /> You and the beast have learned to speak with one voice. Subtract three dice from any roll to resist frenzy. Subtract one die from any roll to resist Detachment. Raise her effective Blood Potency by one dot. She achieves exceptional success on three successes on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Stealth rolls, and gains 8-again. She cannot achieve exceptional successes on Empathy, Expression, Socialize, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls, and loses 10-again.<br /> <br /> Subtract one dice from any roll to resist new Banes<br /> <br /> No longer able to lash out with Competitive or Seductive beast. Lashing out with Monstrous Beast gains 8 again<br /> <br /> Your character will leave The Voice and enter The Second Skin Surrender after one week. This does not give a Beat.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Successfully resist frenzy; if so, leave The Surrender.<br /> <br /> <b>Other Possible Resolution</b>: Gain a dot in Blood Potency, commit Aramanth; if so, enter The Second Skin<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Second Skin (</span>Competitive<span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span><br /> You've learned to share as much ground as possible with the Beast. You wear it just below the surface like a second skin. Subtract five dice from any roll to resist frenzy. Raise her effective Blood Potency by two dots. She achieves exceptional success on three successes on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival and Stealth rolls, and gains 8-again. She cannot achieve exceptional successes on Empathy, Expression, Socialize, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls, and loses 10-again.<br /> <br /> Subtract two dice from any roll to resist Detachment. Subtract two dice from any roll to resist new Banes<br /> <br /> No longer able to lash out with Competitive or Seductive beast. Lashing out with Monstrous Beast gains 8 again<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Gain a dot of Humanity or enter torpor; if so, leave The Black Surrender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","user":"Kevorkiandoctor","date":". 02-17-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}